This project follows a Rails-like structure (app, bin, config, db, lib, tests, tmp). Command `serp` is available providing a number of tools (see `serp -h`). The most routine commands for an ongoing project are
- `serp console`: enter into REPL sync console, like `rails console`;
- `serp db`: enter into REPL db cli (psql), like `rails db`;
- `serp redis`: enter into Redis cli (redis-cli);
- `serp worker`: starts the background jobs worker, this spanws a celery process without the cron, which can be started separately (`serp cron`);
- `serp dbcreate`, `serp dbdrop`: create/drop a database, like `rails db:create`, development environment is assumed if no `APP_ENV` env variable is passed;
- `serp dbload`: loads database schema (creates tables, indexes, functions, etc);
- `serp env`: shows the current `APP_ENV`;
- `serp secret`: generates a random key, like `rails secret`;
- `serp tasks`: list all tasks, like `rails -T`;
- `serp tasks <task_name>`: displays task help info;
- `serp task <task_name>`: executes task synchronously;
- `serp test`: run test suite with PyTest, like `rspec .`
- `serp test path/to/file`, run test(s) matching the path with PyTest.
